//! lotus/compress_env_hold.rye — ALES58: an attack/HOLD/release compressor — the breathing compressor given the one stage between
//! its two knobs. ALES53 gave the compressor (ALES50) a patient sense of time, driving the softened ceiling from ALES52's proven
//! envelope follower so it leans in over the attack and eases the gain back over the release. Yet an un-held compressor still lets
//! its gain jump back toward unity the moment a loud passage momentarily DUCKS below the threshold — it PUMPS, and the ear hears the
//! gain breathe in and out. A real compressor carries a HOLD knob for exactly this: on a fall away from a peak, it pins the peak for
//! a little while before the release begins, so the gain reduction stays engaged through the duck and the level stays steady. ALES56
//! built that hold stage INSIDE the follower (hold_env.env_step_hold) and proved it once. This rung spends that proof: it drives
//! ALES50's softened ceiling from the HELD follower rather than the plain one — the same compressor, now with the patience that keeps
//! it from pumping. The gain math is not re-invented (it is ALES50's), and the time base is not re-invented (it is ALES56's held
//! env_step); this rung is exactly their composition over public APIs, adding only the hold knob. It is the mirror of ALES57's held
//! gate: where the gate's hold keeps the door OPEN across a dip, the compressor's hold keeps the gain reduction ENGAGED across a duck.
//!
//! Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES58.
//! Design read: active-designing/20260814-181719_fill-ales58-lotus-attack-hold-release-compressor.md
//! Stands on: lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2) — the Clip, sample_min/sample_max, max_clip, the range law shape; lotus/compress.rye
//! (ALES50) — the softened ceiling this drives over time, re-proven beside it; lotus/hold_env.rye (ALES56) — the HELD time base, its
//! env_step_hold advancing the same follower one sample at a time with the hold pinning the peak; lotus/compress_env.rye (ALES53) —
//! the un-held attack/release compressor this reduces to at a hold of zero, re-proven beside it as the zero-hold limit.
//!
//! HONEST SCOPE — software only, purely LOCAL. Bounded in-process i16 PCM buffers on one bench, siloed to lotus/. No socket,
//! no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real sample rate — the attack, release, and hold are counted in sample INDICES,
//! not milliseconds against a clock, and the threshold is a magnitude in sample units, the ratio a plain fraction. One held envelope
//! step and at most one multiply-divide per sample; nothing on the path can overflow, since the compressed envelope is at most the
//! envelope so the gain sits in (0, 1] and every written magnitude is at most the input's, which already fits i16.
//!
//!   env RYE_ZIG=vendor/zig-toolchain/zig rye/bin/rye run lotus/compress_env_hold.rye selftest

const std = @import("std");
const assert = std.debug.assert;
const print = std.debug.print;

const timeline = @import("timeline.rye");
const envelope = @import("envelope.rye");
const hold_env = @import("hold_env.rye");
const compress_env = @import("compress_env.rye");

pub const compress_env_hold_version = "20260814.181719";

/// The attack/hold/release compressor's faults, one consistent name each: a threshold outside [1, sample_max], a ratio below unity or
/// with a zero denominator, an attack or release coefficient outside (0, 1], a hold longer than the widest clip, and a span outside
/// the samples. Each coincides by name with the tool it borrows from — BadThreshold and BadRatio from the compressor, BadCoeff from
/// the follower, BadHold from the held follower, BadRange from the whole family — so a composer sees one consistent fault surface.
pub const CompressEnvHoldError = error{
    /// A threshold of zero (no band left to compress below it) or above sample_max (nothing could ever cross it).
    BadThreshold,
    /// A ratio below unity (would expand, not compress) or with a zero denominator — refused, no write.
    BadRatio,
    /// An attack or release coefficient outside (0, 1] — a frozen envelope, an overshooting step, or a divide by zero.
    BadCoeff,
    /// A hold longer than max_clip samples — no clip is that long, so such a hold could never expire within a span; refused, no write.
    BadHold,
    /// A span outside the current samples — refused, no write.
    BadRange,
};

/// Compress `count` samples starting at `start` in place above the magnitude `threshold` by the ratio `ratio_num/ratio_den`, the gain
/// reduction FOLLOWING a HELD envelope that CONTINUES from the caller's `env` and `hold_left` rather than from silence — the
/// carried-state form (ALES43's lesson), now carrying BOTH the envelope and the hold countdown so the hold survives across a call
/// boundary. Each sample advances the proven ALES56 held follower one step (attack while rising and rearming the hold, the peak pinned
/// while the countdown lasts, the release only once it expires); when the held envelope sits within the threshold the sample passes
/// byte-for-byte, and when it rises above, the envelope's excess is divided by the ratio (ALES50's softened ceiling) and that gain
/// applied to the raw sample. With `hold_samples` zero the held follower reduces to ALES52's plain env_step, so this compressor
/// reduces to ALES53's un-held compressor byte-for-byte. Refuses BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadHold, and BadRange before any
/// write; on refusal the clip and the carried state are untouched. Values only — never the length.
pub fn compress_hold_follow_carry(
    clip: *timeline.Clip,
    start: u32,
    count: u32,
    env: *i64,
    hold_left: *u32,
    threshold: i32,
    ratio_num: u32,
    ratio_den: u32,
    attack_num: u32,
    attack_den: u32,
    release_num: u32,
    release_den: u32,
    hold_samples: u32,
) CompressEnvHoldError!void {
    // invariant: the threshold is a legal magnitude — at least one sample unit and no greater than the i16 rail. Before any write.
    if (threshold < 1) return error.BadThreshold;
    if (threshold > @as(i32, timeline.sample_max)) return error.BadThreshold;
    // invariant: the ratio is at least one (num >= den) and its denominator is nonzero — a ratio below one would expand.
    if (ratio_den == 0) return error.BadRatio;
    if (ratio_num < ratio_den) return error.BadRatio;
    // invariant: both attack and release coefficients are legal fractions in (0, 1] — checked by the follower's one proven rule.
    if (!envelope.coeff_ok(attack_num, attack_den)) return error.BadCoeff;
    if (!envelope.coeff_ok(release_num, release_den)) return error.BadCoeff;
    // invariant: the hold is bounded by the widest clip — a longer hold could never expire within any span. Before any write.
    if (hold_samples > timeline.max_clip) return error.BadHold;
    // invariant: the span lies wholly within the current samples — checked without underflow (count vs the remainder).
    if (start > clip.len) return error.BadRange;
    if (count > clip.len - start) return error.BadRange;

    const thr: i64 = @as(i64, threshold);
    const num: i64 = @as(i64, ratio_num);
    const den: i64 = @as(i64, ratio_den);
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < count) : (i += 1) {
        const x: i16 = clip.buf[start + i];
        // Advance the proven ALES56 HELD follower one sample; e is the smoothed-and-held magnitude, in [0, sample_max].
        _ = hold_env.env_step_hold(env, hold_left, x, attack_num, attack_den, release_num, release_den, hold_samples);
        const e: i64 = env.*;
        // invariant: the envelope stays a legal magnitude — never negative, never past the rail (the held step's own guarantee).
        assert(e >= 0 and e <= @as(i64, timeline.sample_max));
        if (e > thr) {
            const excess: i64 = e - thr; // strictly positive: the held detector has crossed the ceiling
            // The compressed envelope target — ALES50's softened ceiling, computed on the ENVELOPE not the bare sample.
            const comp: i64 = thr + @divTrunc(excess * den, num);
            // invariant: the compressed envelope sits within [threshold, envelope] — the gain comp/e is in (0, 1].
            assert(comp >= thr and comp <= e);
            const m: i64 = if (x < 0) -@as(i64, x) else @as(i64, x); // |x| — safe in i64 (|sample_min| = 32768 fits)
            // Apply the gain comp/e to the raw sample. m·comp <= 32768·32767 fits i64; divTrunc keeps it at most m.
            const new_m: i64 = @divTrunc(m * comp, e);
            // invariant: the gain reduces, never boosts — a smoothed compressor only ever leans down.
            assert(new_m <= m);
            const y: i16 = @intCast(if (x < 0) -new_m else new_m); // safe: 0 <= new_m <= m <= 32768 fits i16 by sign
            clip.buf[start + i] = y;
            // invariant: the written sample holds the input's sign (magnitude only shrank).
            assert((x >= 0 and y >= 0) or (x <= 0 and y <= 0));
        }
        // a sample whose held envelope sits within the threshold is left exactly as it was — the gain reduction has not opened; the
        // hold keeping the peak pinned above the threshold is what keeps that reduction engaged across a brief duck rather than pumping.
    }
    // invariant: a compressor changes sample values only, never the clip's length or bound.
    assert(start + count <= clip.len);
    assert(clip.len <= clip.buf.len);
}

/// Compress `count` samples starting at `start` in place, the gain reduction following a HELD envelope that begins FROM SILENCE (a
/// fresh env of 0 with the hold unarmed) — one implementation shared with the carried form, so the two cannot drift. Refuses
/// BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadHold, and BadRange before any write.
pub fn compress_hold_follow(
    clip: *timeline.Clip,
    start: u32,
    count: u32,
    threshold: i32,
    ratio_num: u32,
    ratio_den: u32,
    attack_num: u32,
    attack_den: u32,
    release_num: u32,
    release_den: u32,
    hold_samples: u32,
) CompressEnvHoldError!void {
    var env: i64 = 0;
    var hold_left: u32 = 0;
    return compress_hold_follow_carry(clip, start, count, &env, &hold_left, threshold, ratio_num, ratio_den, attack_num, attack_den, release_num, release_den, hold_samples);
}

// --- selftest: silence stays silence; a HOLD OF ZERO reduces to the plain ALES53 attack/release compressor byte-for-byte (the
//     zero-hold limit); UNIT RATIO is the identity everywhere; a loud signal has its magnitude reduced with the sign held and never
//     expanding; a NONZERO HOLD keeps the gain reduction engaged across a brief duck (it does not pump, the knob monotone); the state
//     CARRIES — env and hold_left both — so a span in two pieces equals the whole once; and a bad threshold, a sub-unity ratio, an
//     illegal coefficient, a hold past max_clip, and an out-of-range span each refuse by name ---------------------------------------

fn eq(got: []const i16, want: []const i16) bool {
    if (got.len != want.len) return false;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < want.len) : (i += 1) if (got[i] != want[i]) return false;
    return true;
}

fn load_clip(clip: *timeline.Clip, src: []const i16) !void {
    try timeline.splice(clip, 0, src);
}

fn abs16(v: i16) i32 {
    return if (v < 0) -@as(i32, v) else @as(i32, v);
}

fn run_selftest() !u8 {
    // 1. silence stays silence — an all-zero clip compresses to all zeros at any legal threshold, ratio, coefficients, and hold.
    {
        var clip = timeline.Clip{};
        try load_clip(&clip, &[_]i16{ 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 });
        try compress_hold_follow(&clip, 0, clip.len, 1000, 4, 1, 1, 4, 1, 8, 3);
        const zeros = [_]i16{ 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 };
        if (!eq(clip.samples(), &zeros)) return error.SilenceWrong;
    }

    // 2. A HOLD OF ZERO IS THE PLAIN ALES53 COMPRESSOR — with hold_samples == 0 the held follower's fall branch never pins, so every
    //    sample moves through ALES52's env_step exactly as ALES53's un-held compressor does: the held compressor with no hold IS the
    //    ALES53 compressor, byte-for-byte by construction. Proven by running BOTH tools on the same signal (the zero-hold limit).
    {
        const loud = [_]i16{ 5000, -5000, 800, -9000, 9000, -200, 32767, -32767, 1200 };
        var held = timeline.Clip{};
        try load_clip(&held, &loud);
        try compress_hold_follow(&held, 0, held.len, 1000, 4, 1, 1, 3, 1, 5, 0); // hold of zero, real attack/release
        var plain = timeline.Clip{};
        try load_clip(&plain, &loud);
        try compress_env.compress_follow(&plain, 0, plain.len, 1000, 4, 1, 1, 3, 1, 5); // the proven ALES53 un-held compressor
        if (!eq(held.samples(), plain.samples())) return error.ZeroHoldNotPlainCompressor;
    }

    // 3. UNIT RATIO IS THE IDENTITY EVERYWHERE — ratio_num == ratio_den makes the compressed envelope equal the envelope, so the gain
    //    is exactly one at every sample regardless of smoothing or hold: the whole signal passes byte-for-byte.
    {
        const loud = [_]i16{ 3000, -3000, 500, -20000, 20000, -400 };
        var clip = timeline.Clip{};
        try load_clip(&clip, &loud);
        try compress_hold_follow(&clip, 0, clip.len, 1000, 3, 3, 1, 4, 1, 8, 4); // unit ratio 3:3, real attack/release, hold 4
        if (!eq(clip.samples(), &loud)) return error.UnitRatioNotIdentity;
    }

    // 4. THE SIGN IS HELD AND THE MAGNITUDE NEVER EXPANDS — a loud signal compresses so every output magnitude is at most the input's
    //    and every sign matches, under a real attack, release, and hold.
    {
        const loud = [_]i16{ 6000, -6000, 800, -12000, 12000, -300, 9000, -9000 };
        var clip = timeline.Clip{};
        try load_clip(&clip, &loud);
        try compress_hold_follow(&clip, 0, clip.len, 1000, 4, 1, 1, 2, 1, 6, 2);
        const out = clip.samples();
        var i: u32 = 0;
        while (i < out.len) : (i += 1) {
            if (abs16(out[i]) > abs16(loud[i])) return error.MagnitudeExpanded; // the gain only ever reduces
            if ((loud[i] > 0 and out[i] < 0) or (loud[i] < 0 and out[i] > 0)) return error.SignFlipped;
        }
    }

    // 5. A NONZERO HOLD KEEPS THE GAIN REDUCTION ENGAGED ACROSS A BRIEF DUCK — a loud sample, one quiet duck below the threshold, then
    //    loud again. With INSTANT attack and INSTANT release and NO hold, the duck drops the envelope below the threshold so the gain
    //    reduction disengages and the duck passes byte-for-byte (the compressor PUMPS — its gain jumped back to unity). With a hold
    //    that spans the duck, the peak stays pinned above the threshold so the gain reduction stays engaged and the duck is
    //    attenuated. So the held magnitude is no LARGER than the un-held one at every sample (the hold only ever keeps the gain DOWN,
    //    the knob monotone in the compressor's direction), and strictly QUIETER at the duck (the pumping avoided).
    {
        const duck = [_]i16{ 15000, 300, 15000 }; // loud, a quiet duck below threshold, loud again
        const thr: i32 = 1000;
        var none = timeline.Clip{};
        try load_clip(&none, &duck);
        try compress_hold_follow(&none, 0, none.len, thr, 4, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0); // instant attack, instant release, no hold
        var held = timeline.Clip{};
        try load_clip(&held, &duck);
        try compress_hold_follow(&held, 0, held.len, thr, 4, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1); // same, hold of 1 spans the single duck sample
        var i: u32 = 0;
        while (i < duck.len) : (i += 1) {
            if (abs16(held.samples()[i]) > abs16(none.samples()[i])) return error.HoldPumpedMore;
        }
        // the duck sample (index 1): the held compressor keeps the pinned peak above threshold so the gain reduction stays engaged and
        // attenuates it, the un-held compressor has already released to unity and passes it whole — the hold avoided the pump.
        if (abs16(held.samples()[1]) >= abs16(none.samples()[1])) return error.HoldDidNotEngage;
    }

    // 6. THE STATE CARRIES — env AND hold_left both — so compressing a span in two pieces, the split falling MID-HOLD, equals
    //    compressing the whole once, byte-for-byte: the seam invisible, so dynamics can span and automate.
    {
        const sig = [_]i16{ 14000, 14000, 400, 400, 400, 9000, 6000, 6000 };
        var whole = timeline.Clip{};
        try load_clip(&whole, &sig);
        try compress_hold_follow(&whole, 0, whole.len, 1000, 4, 1, 1, 1, 1, 5, 2);

        var split = timeline.Clip{};
        try load_clip(&split, &sig);
        var env: i64 = 0;
        var hold_left: u32 = 0;
        try compress_hold_follow_carry(&split, 0, 3, &env, &hold_left, 1000, 4, 1, 1, 1, 1, 5, 2); // first piece — split at index 3 mid-hold
        try compress_hold_follow_carry(&split, 3, split.len - 3, &env, &hold_left, 1000, 4, 1, 1, 1, 1, 5, 2); // second continues env AND hold_left
        if (!eq(split.samples(), whole.samples())) return error.CarryNotEqual;
    }

    // 7a. a zero threshold refuses BadThreshold before any write, the clip untouched.
    {
        var clip = timeline.Clip{};
        const three = [_]i16{ 1, 2, 3 };
        try load_clip(&clip, &three);
        if (compress_hold_follow(&clip, 0, clip.len, 0, 4, 1, 1, 4, 1, 8, 2)) |_| return error.ZeroThresholdSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadThreshold) return error.WrongZeroThreshold;
        if (!eq(clip.samples(), &three)) return error.RefusedThresholdMutated;
    }

    // 7b. a sub-unity ratio (would expand) refuses BadRatio before any write.
    {
        var clip = timeline.Clip{};
        const three = [_]i16{ 1, 2, 3 };
        try load_clip(&clip, &three);
        if (compress_hold_follow(&clip, 0, clip.len, 1000, 1, 2, 1, 4, 1, 8, 2)) |_| return error.SubUnitySlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadRatio) return error.WrongSubUnity;
        if (!eq(clip.samples(), &three)) return error.RefusedRatioMutated;
    }

    // 7c. an illegal attack coefficient (numerator past the denominator) refuses BadCoeff before any write.
    {
        var clip = timeline.Clip{};
        const three = [_]i16{ 1, 2, 3 };
        try load_clip(&clip, &three);
        if (compress_hold_follow(&clip, 0, clip.len, 1000, 4, 1, 3, 2, 1, 8, 2)) |_| return error.BadAttackSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadCoeff) return error.WrongBadAttack;
        if (!eq(clip.samples(), &three)) return error.RefusedCoeffMutated;
    }

    // 7d. a hold longer than max_clip (no clip is that long) refuses BadHold before any write.
    {
        var clip = timeline.Clip{};
        const three = [_]i16{ 1, 2, 3 };
        try load_clip(&clip, &three);
        if (compress_hold_follow(&clip, 0, clip.len, 1000, 4, 1, 1, 4, 1, 8, timeline.max_clip + 1)) |_| return error.BadHoldSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadHold) return error.WrongBadHold;
        if (!eq(clip.samples(), &three)) return error.RefusedHoldMutated;
    }

    // 7e. an out-of-range span refuses BadRange before any write, leaving the clip untouched.
    {
        var clip = timeline.Clip{};
        const three = [_]i16{ 1, 2, 3 };
        try load_clip(&clip, &three);
        if (compress_hold_follow(&clip, 2, 5, 1000, 4, 1, 1, 4, 1, 8, 2)) |_| return error.BadRangeSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadRange) return error.WrongBadRange;
        if (!eq(clip.samples(), &three)) return error.RefusedRangeMutated;
    }

    print("GREEN ales-compress-env-hold: an attack/HOLD/release compressor drives ALES50's softened ceiling from ALES56's HELD " ++
        "envelope — each sample advances the held follower one step (attack rising and rearming the hold, the peak pinned while the " ++
        "countdown lasts, the release only once it expires), and when the held envelope crosses the threshold its excess is divided " ++
        "by the ratio and that gain applied to the raw sample. Silence stays silence; a HOLD OF ZERO reduces to the plain ALES53 " ++
        "attack/release compressor BYTE-FOR-BYTE (the zero-hold limit, proven by running both tools); UNIT RATIO is the identity " ++
        "everywhere; a loud signal has its magnitude reduced with the sign held and never expanding; a NONZERO HOLD keeps the gain " ++
        "reduction engaged across a brief duck (it does not pump, the knob monotone); the state CARRIES — env and hold_left both — " ++
        "so a span in two pieces equals the whole once (the seam invisible, the hold surviving the boundary); and a zero threshold " ++
        "refuses BadThreshold, a sub-unity ratio BadRatio, an illegal coefficient BadCoeff, a hold past max_clip BadHold, an " ++
        "out-of-range span BadRange, each leaving the clip untouched; no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no " ++
        "real sample rate\n", .{});
    return 0;
}

pub fn main(init: std.process.Init) !u8 {
    _ = init;
    return run_selftest();
}
